    {
      "path": "law/schemas/api-map.schema.json",
      "sha256": "26df9ef84ee9c2ebb0d1d01690919988069f3185801e5c44a003452e1176bcd3",
      "jsonPointer": "/$defs/Auth/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Static auth/guard declarations, not proof of complete permission semantics. required=false needs an explicit recognized public marker; missing static Permission metadata never means public. Conditional/unresolved guard permissions remain unresolved (ADR-SCR-0016).",
      "reference": "ADR-SCR-0016",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 250,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "$defs",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "$defs",
          "Auth"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/api-map.schema.json",
      "sha256": "26df9ef84ee9c2ebb0d1d01690919988069f3185801e5c44a003452e1176bcd3",
      "jsonPointer": "/$defs/Endpoint/properties/id/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Unique endpoint observation identity shared by API, coverage, RBAC and HTTP-evidence consumers (ADR-SCR-0016). The producer emits api:v1: followed by encodeURIComponent of canonical JSON [method,path,controller,evidence], with portable paths and canonically sorted evidence. This preserves source variants, not a claim that every variant is mounted simultaneously. Evidence lines are part of identity; source movement can require authored reference migration. Existing explicit IDs remain readable only when unique and nonconflicting.",
      "reference": "ADR-SCR-0016",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 96,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "$defs",
          "properties",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "$defs",
          "Endpoint",
          "properties",
          "id"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/backlog-item.schema.json",
      "sha256": "194087c8948d8381ee92e79a3b60e3e67e56a9c3058a4a8ace8c429e33014c38",
      "jsonPointer": "/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "One schema-validated record under .devai/state/backlog/ written by the backlog action family (ADR-GOV-0019): a finding discovered during work that belongs to no round, a proposition for a later session, a note from one agent to another, or a flaky test observed under ADR-CHK-0001. An item carries its origin session, role, and commit so it outlives the session that made it. Round attribution is optional and is never inferred. A backlog item is not a round gap: it cannot pause, resolve, or otherwise alter one.",
      "reference": "ADR-GOV-0019",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 94,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": []
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/backlog-item.schema.json",
