    {
      "path": "law/schemas/campaign.schema.json",
      "sha256": "23d38995312663cb486a1af7ce3b5818c6c198c4caf1fe50fc0c1c0f5b992747",
      "jsonPointer": "/properties/models/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Optional override of the repository default in law/policy/model-tiers.json, by tier name (ADR-MDL-0002). A tier the block does not name resolves to the default; an unknown tier name, an effort outside the tier grammar, or a host the default does not declare fails closed at the campaign check. A campaign never introduces a host. A closed campaign keeps its block byte-for-byte as evidence. Tiers are the only names prompts and tasks use; the host models behind a tier change in the default, not in a prompt.",
      "reference": "ADR-MDL-0002",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 90,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "properties",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "properties",
          "models"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/campaign.schema.json",
      "sha256": "23d38995312663cb486a1af7ce3b5818c6c198c4caf1fe50fc0c1c0f5b992747",
      "jsonPointer": "/properties/review/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Which of the four review steps of law/policy/campaign-execution.json gates.review the campaign delegates to a model (ADR-GOV-0023). Absent, the campaign resolves to human. Gate ratification, merge, and dispatch of any remote effect are human in every mode.",
      "reference": "ADR-GOV-0023",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 117,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "properties",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "properties",
          "review"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/check-suites.schema.json",
      "sha256": "a9da457849b7b55b6fa25c6f8e81adc034e46c47d29392a16ff499020c93f248",
      "jsonPointer": "/$defs/applicability/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Where the member applies (ADR-CHK-0005): `self` reads only the DEVAI source repository's own law, policy, scripts, or catalogue and reports not-applicable in an adopter; `adopter` reads only an adopter repository; `both` reads the checked repository whichever kind it is.",
      "reference": "ADR-CHK-0005",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 26,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "$defs",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "$defs",
          "applicability"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/check-suites.schema.json",
      "sha256": "a9da457849b7b55b6fa25c6f8e81adc034e46c47d29392a16ff499020c93f248",
      "jsonPointer": "/properties/selector_definitions/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Applicability declarations for the `check --only` selectors that are dispatched by the CLI without a suite member definition (ADR-CHK-0005). Every selector the CLI accepts declares exactly one entry; a selector without a declaration is not dispatchable.",
      "reference": "ADR-CHK-0005",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 126,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "properties",
          "description"
        ],
