    {
      "path": "law/schemas/model-tiers.schema.json",
      "sha256": "4e330680f6c0d0fef5562584d34f43c0a697c04111fa50c3eeff0504eaf99a21",
      "jsonPointer": "/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Contract for law/policy/model-tiers.json, the repository default of the campaign models block under ADR-MDL-0002. The document declares the hosts a campaign may run on, each with the runtime bridge from law/policy/model-runtime-registry.json it resolves through and the model aliases that host publishes; the tiers with their rank, one alias per declared host keyed by host id, a default effort, and a use_for text; the Article 19 escalation rule; and a policy_version. A campaign overrides the default by tier name only and never introduces a host. The resolved map is pinned on each task at task_start together with policy_version, so a later change to this document never reinterprets a started task. The default is law and changes only through a law commit that bumps policy_version.",
      "reference": "ADR-MDL-0002",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 100,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": []
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/mutation-evidence-policy-v2.schema.json",
      "sha256": "80e0debbc35368edd3fa1b000ad5627f8aa109aa79af98613169450c204318af",
      "jsonPointer": "/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Exact source-pinned active policy contract for the sole forward mutation-v2 protocol. Every value is frozen by ADR-MUT-0007. Emission and verification additionally require runtime recomputation of the pinned vendor manifest, exact file population and byte-set equality; schema validity alone grants no activation.",
      "reference": "ADR-MUT-0007",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 111,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": []
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/native-service-profile.schema.json",
      "sha256": "8b3f5f181adb6e727d2e14c5e8b8aa398d21d41f77344a055b65f7e16cf8f698",
      "jsonPointer": "/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Forward opt-in native fixture request under resultPopulation.serviceProfile. This declaration grants no authority or readiness. A package-owned planner must bind exact toolchain/artifact identities and independently prove provisioning, contained transports and terminal cleanup before execution origin or standing (ADR-SCR-0020). No caller endpoints, sockets, secrets, command strings, roots or origin tokens are accepted.",
      "reference": "ADR-SCR-0020",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 315,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": []
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/observation-backlog.schema.json",
      "sha256": "dd838e27a2ef363b95fa45255f73e2a32c63f389980cdb95254ffa4d2435dd87",
      "jsonPointer": "/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "The backlog.json that audit observe writes into a post-merge observation bundle (ADR-SCR-0008, Article 33): the observed merge sha, the timestamp, one observation per scorecard cell with its verdict and the ids of the readings it was composed from, and the deltas against the previous bundle. The object is closed at every level, so an unknown top-level key fails; an observation without its cell fails; and a delta names a cell by the same coordinate grammar as the N/A ledger. A delta that names a cell absent from the current observations is rejected by the validating suite, which cross-checks the two arrays, because the cross-reference is outside what JSON Schema expresses.",
      "reference": "ADR-SCR-0008",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 81,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": []
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/path-authority-classes.schema.json",
      "sha256": "1d1740d2149023705435f52230c352c7dd5111722eddd2271945cd885d667a7b",
      "jsonPointer": "/$defs/selector/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "One root-relative minimatch glob under the ADR-AUT-0003 grammar: no leading `/`, `!`, or `#`; no `.` or `..` segment; no backslash; no `//`; no trailing `/`; no brace; no extglob. The compiler additionally refuses a selector whose first segment equals a declared root (ADOPTER_AUTHORITY_SELECTOR_ROOTED), which no default can satisfy for every adopter and is therefore checked at bind.",
      "reference": "ADR-AUT-0003",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 43,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "$defs",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "$defs",
          "selector"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/path-authority-classes.schema.json",
      "sha256": "1d1740d2149023705435f52230c352c7dd5111722eddd2271945cd885d667a7b",
      "jsonPointer": "/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "The package default path-class selectors of ADR-AUT-0003, declared as a law source at law/policy/adopter-defaults/path-authority-classes.json. An adopter authority block that omits classes.test takes its Inspector test-class selectors from this file; the architecture class has no default and cannot be declared here, so an adopter that wants Architect classes under its roots names them in its own source. Every selector obeys the root-relative selector grammar of the record: a minimatch glob applied under every declared root, never absolute, never starting with a root segment, and free of dot segments, backslashes, doubled or trailing separators, braces, and extglobs. The bind compiles each selector under each declared root; nothing here names a root.",
      "reference": "ADR-AUT-0003",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 44,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": []
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/path-authority-classes.schema.json",
      "sha256": "1d1740d2149023705435f52230c352c7dd5111722eddd2271945cd885d667a7b",
      "jsonPointer": "/properties/classes/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "The classes that carry a package default. Only test is admitted: ADR-AUT-0003 gives the architecture class no default, so DDL coverage is explicit in each adopter's source and testable.",
      "reference": "ADR-AUT-0003",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 65,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "properties",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "properties",
          "classes"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/preflight-probe.schema.json",
      "sha256": "7db00223a31060ebde21512bfdb5dd95ebbf53bdf81c41e651ed48f4c86beb8e",
      "jsonPointer": "/$defs/credential_probe/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Confirms a credential named by the credential manifest (ADR-SEC-0001) is present without reading its value into any report.",
      "reference": "ADR-SEC-0001",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 56,
      "context": {
