    {
      "path": "law/schemas/review-verdict.schema.json",
      "sha256": "c47b3b45218663d63f23162c73b2cfe010045ba841fcae1ff4d3bd85eb726f35",
      "jsonPointer": "/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "The document a model-evaluated review reply must carry under ADR-MDL-0001. Two consumers validate it through the one shared extractor in the model bridge: the llm_judge sensor (packages/sensors/src/judge.ts), which maps the verdict onto its reading status, and the campaign model_evaluation step that ADR-GOV-0023 admits, where the orchestrator records the extracted document on the task review block together with the SHA-256 of the full reply. The extractor accepts a provider json field or exactly one unambiguous candidate object in the reply text, fenced or not, and returns either a document that validates here or an error outcome with a bounded redacted excerpt and the reply digest; it never returns a partial document and never guesses between candidates. The document is closed so a triage classification, an echoed example with extra members, or any other shape is refused. The verdict vocabulary is the sensor-reading status subset the judge emits: the execution status core plus unknown, the explicit uncertainty of Constitution Article 39, so it is declared locally rather than through common-defs.",
      "reference": "ADR-MDL-0001",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 61,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": []
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/review-verdict.schema.json",
      "sha256": "c47b3b45218663d63f23162c73b2cfe010045ba841fcae1ff4d3bd85eb726f35",
      "jsonPointer": "/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "The document a model-evaluated review reply must carry under ADR-MDL-0001. Two consumers validate it through the one shared extractor in the model bridge: the llm_judge sensor (packages/sensors/src/judge.ts), which maps the verdict onto its reading status, and the campaign model_evaluation step that ADR-GOV-0023 admits, where the orchestrator records the extracted document on the task review block together with the SHA-256 of the full reply. The extractor accepts a provider json field or exactly one unambiguous candidate object in the reply text, fenced or not, and returns either a document that validates here or an error outcome with a bounded redacted excerpt and the reply digest; it never returns a partial document and never guesses between candidates. The document is closed so a triage classification, an echoed example with extra members, or any other shape is refused. The verdict vocabulary is the sensor-reading status subset the judge emits: the execution status core plus unknown, the explicit uncertainty of Constitution Article 39, so it is declared locally rather than through common-defs.",
      "reference": "ADR-GOV-0023",
      "occurrenceIndex": 1,
      "stringOffset": 301,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": []
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/reviewed-workflow-steps.schema.json",
      "sha256": "9f8f3172a9a5850d92223d9f9772f5b146e5bf8f59d3196b40766120b0dc0641",
      "jsonPointer": "/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Complete optional adopter-owned reviewed step effects projected only by registered binding. Canonical YAML, exact occurrences and complete executable/import closure must match; no entry changes permissions or grants execution authority (ADR-SCR-0017).",
      "reference": "ADR-SCR-0017",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 237,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": []
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/round-execution.schema.json",
      "sha256": "9b9719276e1c2576758cf404c6554a5e29c799421750ec3c8a06a1db1948e3f5",
      "jsonPointer": "/properties/capacity/properties/review_reserve/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Workers kept for review-discipline tasks (ADR-MDL-0009). While a same-generation review task awaits admission, non-review tasks may occupy at most the run's workers minus reserved_workers; review tasks may use every worker. A serial run, or one with no more workers than the reserve, is unreserved.",
      "reference": "ADR-MDL-0009",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 42,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "properties",
          "properties",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "properties",
          "capacity",
          "properties",
          "review_reserve"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/self-dogfood-policy.schema.json",
      "sha256": "d9b0cf65f83422545b44951c7376fc4c8adc3527d799d636643e6f8015e8e303",
      "jsonPointer": "/$defs/permitted_check/properties/harness_write_paths/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "The repository paths a harness-write check is declared to write, relative to the repository root. ADR-SCR-0008 requires sense record to declare the chain path beside the readings directory, so its two ordered writes (the reading file, then the sense.readings.record chain entry) are both declared harness-writes.",
      "reference": "ADR-SCR-0008",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 98,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "$defs",
          "properties",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "$defs",
          "permitted_check",
          "properties",
          "harness_write_paths"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/self-dogfood-policy.schema.json",
      "sha256": "d9b0cf65f83422545b44951c7376fc4c8adc3527d799d636643e6f8015e8e303",
      "jsonPointer": "/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Contract for DEVAI running its own governed checks against the DEVAI source repository. Self-consumption is verification configuration only: every run is human-invoked, no run performs autonomous work, no run widens a role, and no run carries publication authority. The role and effect matrix states, per role, exactly which effects a self-dogfood run may initiate; remote-write is forbidden for every role without exception. The check roster and the role rows are frozen by position and by exact value, so a duplicated, reordered, or substituted identifier, effect, or role fails rather than resolving to the entry it resembles. ADR-SCR-0001 admits three sensing actions by addition: sense run with a read effect for every role, and sense record and audit observe with a harness-write effect for the inspector only. The harness-write sensing actions are structurally limited to rows that permit harness-write, and no sensing action carries a remote effect.",
      "reference": "ADR-SCR-0001",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 630,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": []
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/sensor-inputs.schema.json",
      "sha256": "5369a80c338b0a7a586e60f1e7e9bb0d29f2fbcdea0427a6ab51046af5df98a2",
      "jsonPointer": "/$defs/build_inputs/properties/argv/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Build command the sensor executes, without a shell, and grades by exit code, for an adopter whose repository has no test-tasks.json build node (ADR-AUT-0002). When the descriptor carries a build node that node's argv and cwd are the command and this declaration is not admitted; a declaration whose argv differs from the node is a declaration defect read as error with BUILD_ARGV_CONFLICT. Under sense run the authority broker admits only the build shape law/policy/subprocess-effects.json declares (pnpm-recursive-build); a declared argv outside it is refused before a process starts.",
      "reference": "ADR-AUT-0002",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 144,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "$defs",
          "properties",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "$defs",
          "build_inputs",
          "properties",
          "argv"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/sensor-inputs.schema.json",
      "sha256": "5369a80c338b0a7a586e60f1e7e9bb0d29f2fbcdea0427a6ab51046af5df98a2",
      "jsonPointer": "/$defs/harness_population_inputs/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "The CI population one harness sensor samples (ADR-SCR-0010): which workflow and event, on which head and base branch, which attempts, whether cancelled runs count, how far back, how many runs make a verdict, and which workflow-and-job pairs are left out by identity. The population is part of the reading's metrics. Below minimumSample the sensor reads unknown with the sample size, the minimum, and the population in its finding, never pass and never fail; at or above it the verdict is the measured one under the sensor's existing thresholds. Declaring a population never changes a threshold.",
      "reference": "ADR-SCR-0010",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 46,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "$defs",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "$defs",
          "harness_population_inputs"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/sensor-inputs.schema.json",
      "sha256": "5369a80c338b0a7a586e60f1e7e9bb0d29f2fbcdea0427a6ab51046af5df98a2",
      "jsonPointer": "/$defs/harness_population_inputs/properties/outcomeUnit/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "harness_green_main only (ADR-SCR-0014): what one outcome is. run counts every sampled run, the population of ADR-SCR-0010. pull-request-final-head counts one outcome per pull request against the base with a sampled run in the lookback window, merged, closed without merge, or open: the latest completed run whose conclusion is neither cancelled nor skipped on the pull request's final head (the head at merge, or the current head), matched by head branch and sha; an open pull request without such a run is excluded. Default run when omitted. harness_performance and harness_robustness refuse the property.",
      "reference": "ADR-SCR-0014",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 25,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "$defs",
          "properties",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "$defs",
          "harness_population_inputs",
          "properties",
          "outcomeUnit"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/sensor-inputs.schema.json",
      "sha256": "5369a80c338b0a7a586e60f1e7e9bb0d29f2fbcdea0427a6ab51046af5df98a2",
      "jsonPointer": "/$defs/harness_population_inputs/properties/outcomeUnit/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "harness_green_main only (ADR-SCR-0014): what one outcome is. run counts every sampled run, the population of ADR-SCR-0010. pull-request-final-head counts one outcome per pull request against the base with a sampled run in the lookback window, merged, closed without merge, or open: the latest completed run whose conclusion is neither cancelled nor skipped on the pull request's final head (the head at merge, or the current head), matched by head branch and sha; an open pull request without such a run is excluded. Default run when omitted. harness_performance and harness_robustness refuse the property.",
      "reference": "ADR-SCR-0010",
      "occurrenceIndex": 1,
      "stringOffset": 109,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "$defs",
          "properties",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "$defs",
          "harness_population_inputs",
          "properties",
          "outcomeUnit"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/sensor-inputs.schema.json",
      "sha256": "5369a80c338b0a7a586e60f1e7e9bb0d29f2fbcdea0427a6ab51046af5df98a2",
      "jsonPointer": "/$defs/perf_test_inputs/properties/argv/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Performance suite command the sensor executes, without a shell, and grades by exit code, duration, and an optional JSON metrics line. When declared it takes precedence over scriptName. Under sense run the authority broker admits only the governed pnpm vitest run --config <governed-config> [<test-path>] shape and exactly pnpm test:perf (templates pnpm-vitest-run-governed-config and pnpm-test-perf, ADR-AUT-0006); any other argv, including node <script> or pnpm run test:perf, is refused before a process starts.",
      "reference": "ADR-AUT-0006",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 400,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "$defs",
          "properties",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "$defs",
          "perf_test_inputs",
          "properties",
          "argv"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/sensor-inputs.schema.json",
      "sha256": "5369a80c338b0a7a586e60f1e7e9bb0d29f2fbcdea0427a6ab51046af5df98a2",
      "jsonPointer": "/$defs/perf_test_inputs/properties/scriptName/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Legacy key: the root package script the sensor runs as pnpm <scriptName> when no argv is declared, instead of the sensor default of test:perf. Under sense run the broker admits only the default, pnpm test:perf (ADR-AUT-0006); any other script name is refused before a process starts.",
      "reference": "ADR-AUT-0006",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 211,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "$defs",
          "properties",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "$defs",
          "perf_test_inputs",
          "properties",
          "scriptName"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/sensor-inputs.schema.json",
      "sha256": "5369a80c338b0a7a586e60f1e7e9bb0d29f2fbcdea0427a6ab51046af5df98a2",
      "jsonPointer": "/$defs/surfaces/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "The plant surfaces the repository declares (ADR-SCR-0003). Every surface is stated, true or false. A sensor bound only to absent surfaces emits skipped with the declaration as its reason and its cell records N/A when every reading there is skipped; a sensor that finds evidence of an absent surface reports review instead of skipping. When this object is omitted every surface is presumed present and each sensor measures as it did before the declaration existed.",
      "reference": "ADR-SCR-0003",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 44,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "$defs",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "$defs",
          "surfaces"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/sensor-inputs.schema.json",
      "sha256": "5369a80c338b0a7a586e60f1e7e9bb0d29f2fbcdea0427a6ab51046af5df98a2",
      "jsonPointer": "/$defs/test_coverage_depth_inputs/properties/coveragePath/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Istanbul per-file coverage report (coverage-final.json shape) the sensor normalizes, instead of the sensor default of coverage/coverage-final.json. When the report is absent the sensor runs the declared producer for the population and reads the report it writes; a producer that exits non-zero reads FAIL with its exit code, and a report still missing after a zero exit reads FAIL with COVERAGE_REPORT_MISSING (ADR-SCR-0007).",
      "reference": "ADR-SCR-0007",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 411,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "$defs",
          "properties",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "$defs",
          "test_coverage_depth_inputs",
          "properties",
          "coveragePath"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/sensor-inputs.schema.json",
      "sha256": "5369a80c338b0a7a586e60f1e7e9bb0d29f2fbcdea0427a6ab51046af5df98a2",
      "jsonPointer": "/$defs/test_coverage_depth_inputs/properties/exclusions/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Repository-relative test files the declared population leaves out, named one by one (ADR-SCR-0007): for the local population, the RC-only and database-bound suites that tests/config/local.config.ts lists as RC_ONLY. The sensor refuses a report whose sidecar lists a different exclusion set with the mismatch named. Declaring an exclusion changes the denominator the reading states, never a threshold.",
      "reference": "ADR-SCR-0007",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 85,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "$defs",
          "properties",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "$defs",
          "test_coverage_depth_inputs",
          "properties",
          "exclusions"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/sensor-inputs.schema.json",
      "sha256": "5369a80c338b0a7a586e60f1e7e9bb0d29f2fbcdea0427a6ab51046af5df98a2",
      "jsonPointer": "/$defs/test_coverage_depth_inputs/properties/population/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Name of the test population the report measures (ADR-SCR-0007): local is the LOCAL_INCLUDE population produced by tests/config/local.coverage.config.ts without a database; rc is the full population the RC coverage gate produces behind DEVAI_DB_TESTS. The producer writes a population.json sidecar beside the report naming its population, include globs, excluded suites, and measured file count; the sensor refuses a report whose sidecar names another population, so a stale report of one population is never read as the measurement of another, and every reading states the population it measured in metrics and in its finding text.",
      "reference": "ADR-SCR-0007",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 49,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "$defs",
          "properties",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "$defs",
          "test_coverage_depth_inputs",
          "properties",
          "population"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/sensor-inputs.schema.json",
      "sha256": "5369a80c338b0a7a586e60f1e7e9bb0d29f2fbcdea0427a6ab51046af5df98a2",
      "jsonPointer": "/$defs/test_suite_inputs/properties/argv/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Test suite command the sensor executes, without a shell, and grades by exit code and the vitest summary line, instead of the sensor default of pnpm vitest run --config tests/config/t1.unit.config.ts, t3.integration.config.ts, or t5.e2e.config.ts for the unit, integration, or end-to-end suite. Under sense run the broker admits only the governed shape of template pnpm-vitest-run-governed-config in law/policy/subprocess-effects.json; the framework's e2e_test declares tests/config/rc.e2e.config.ts, whose own include selects tests/e2e, with no test path appended (ADR-SCR-0007).",
      "reference": "ADR-SCR-0007",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 565,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "$defs",
          "properties",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "$defs",
          "test_suite_inputs",
          "properties",
          "argv"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/sensor-inputs.schema.json",
      "sha256": "5369a80c338b0a7a586e60f1e7e9bb0d29f2fbcdea0427a6ab51046af5df98a2",
      "jsonPointer": "/$defs/type_check_inputs/properties/argv/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Type check command the sensor executes, without a shell, instead of its default of npx tsc --noEmit against the root tsconfig; its diagnostics are parsed the same way. Under sense run the authority broker admits only npx tsc --noEmit, npx tsc --noEmit -p <relative path>, and exactly pnpm -r typecheck for a pnpm workspace (templates npx-tsc-noemit, npx-tsc-noemit-project, and pnpm-recursive-typecheck, ADR-AUT-0006); any other argv, including pnpm typecheck, pnpm run typecheck, or an added argument, is refused before a process starts.",
      "reference": "ADR-AUT-0006",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 404,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "$defs",
          "properties",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "$defs",
          "type_check_inputs",
          "properties",
          "argv"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/sensor-inputs.schema.json",
      "sha256": "5369a80c338b0a7a586e60f1e7e9bb0d29f2fbcdea0427a6ab51046af5df98a2",
      "jsonPointer": "/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "One adopter-owned declaration of the inputs its sensors read and the plant surfaces it has, materialized at .devai/config/sensor-inputs.json from the law default under law/policy/adopter-defaults/sensor-inputs.json (ADR-SCR-0005, ADR-SCR-0003). Every entry under inputs is keyed by a registered sensor kind from law/policy/sensor-registry.json and carries only the inputs that kind reads: test roots, the decision record directory, the invariants directory, the coverage report path with its measured population and exclusion list (ADR-SCR-0007), the effects tsconfig path, the type check argv, the unit, integration, and end-to-end suite argv, the performance suite argv or legacy script name, the build argv and optional working directory, the reusable-workflow threshold, the plant depth exclusion globs, and the CI population of the three harness sensors (workflow, event, head and base branch, attempts, cancelled runs, lookback, minimum sample, excluded workflow-and-job pairs; ADR-SCR-0010). A kind that declares nothing keeps the sensor's own default; the build input is admitted only when test-tasks.json has no build node, and a build declaration whose argv differs from that node reads error with BUILD_ARGV_CONFLICT (ADR-AUT-0002); sense run refuses a key this schema does not list, a kind the registry does not hold, and a path that leaves the repository root, and merges an explicit --input for the same key over the declaration for one run only. The surfaces object names which of the four plant surfaces the repository has (http, database, rbac, actions), each true or false; a sensor bound only to surfaces declared absent emits a skipped reading carrying the declaration as its reason, the scorecard composer records a cell whose readings are all skipped as N/A with that reason, and a sensor that finds a surface declared absent reports review. Declaring an input never changes a threshold or a verdict rule. ADR-SCR-0015 adds policy-owned projection, explicit Angular/React route inputs, and exact descriptor task references. Task references are not arbitrary command admission.",
      "reference": "ADR-SCR-0005",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 216,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": []
      }
    },
    {
