      "jsonPointer": "/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "One adopter-owned declaration of the inputs its sensors read and the plant surfaces it has, materialized at .devai/config/sensor-inputs.json from the law default under law/policy/adopter-defaults/sensor-inputs.json (ADR-SCR-0005, ADR-SCR-0003). Every entry under inputs is keyed by a registered sensor kind from law/policy/sensor-registry.json and carries only the inputs that kind reads: test roots, the decision record directory, the invariants directory, the coverage report path with its measured population and exclusion list (ADR-SCR-0007), the effects tsconfig path, the type check argv, the unit, integration, and end-to-end suite argv, the performance suite argv or legacy script name, the build argv and optional working directory, the reusable-workflow threshold, the plant depth exclusion globs, and the CI population of the three harness sensors (workflow, event, head and base branch, attempts, cancelled runs, lookback, minimum sample, excluded workflow-and-job pairs; ADR-SCR-0010). A kind that declares nothing keeps the sensor's own default; the build input is admitted only when test-tasks.json has no build node, and a build declaration whose argv differs from that node reads error with BUILD_ARGV_CONFLICT (ADR-AUT-0002); sense run refuses a key this schema does not list, a kind the registry does not hold, and a path that leaves the repository root, and merges an explicit --input for the same key over the declaration for one run only. The surfaces object names which of the four plant surfaces the repository has (http, database, rbac, actions), each true or false; a sensor bound only to surfaces declared absent emits a skipped reading carrying the declaration as its reason, the scorecard composer records a cell whose readings are all skipped as N/A with that reason, and a sensor that finds a surface declared absent reports review. Declaring an input never changes a threshold or a verdict rule. ADR-SCR-0015 adds policy-owned projection, expl