    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/sensor-reading.schema.json",
      "sha256": "bdf104d7739623c09acf4c1e2531afc527779ebd7905831d7ea0b641e7c6f7c8",
      "jsonPointer": "/properties/supersedes/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "The id of the earlier recorded instance of the same kind for the same candidate that this reading replaces (ADR-SCR-0008). A recorded reading is immutable, so a later reading is a new instance that names the earlier one here; the scorecard selects the latest instance by following these links, never by file time. A reading with no earlier instance omits the field.",
      "reference": "ADR-SCR-0008",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 108,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "properties",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "properties",
          "supersedes"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/sensor-registry.schema.json",
      "sha256": "6ef8757e6b0f9d412cec529e8f67bf50a1b489c89e66562d02d30a066fb34175",
      "jsonPointer": "/$defs/entry/properties/schema_admission/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Schema admission of this kind under ADR-SCR-0011. Absent or admitted: the kind must be in the sensor.kind enum of the packaged law/schemas/sensor-reading.schema.json, and every kind a preset can select is admitted. unsupported: the runner refuses the sensor before it starts with SENSOR_KIND_SCHEMA_UNSUPPORTED and never emits a reading for it.",
      "reference": "ADR-SCR-0011",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 36,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "$defs",
          "properties",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "$defs",
          "entry",
          "properties",
          "schema_admission"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/soft-gate-rubric.schema.json",
      "sha256": "d6aa87ba28d06d1e282d2c4235c5ca3a1cb627f95620a308e914c786bacfd039",
      "jsonPointer": "/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "The Architect-owned rubric the scored llm_judge mode of ADR-MDL-0004 gives the evaluator, separate from the generic review-verdict contract. It names the four soft dimensions spec_coherence, plant_idiomaticity, test_depth and traceability_quality, each with up to 32 deterministic criteria the evaluator must observe and cite, and fixes the meaning of every integer score level 0 to 4. Aggregation is all-dimensions: each dimension is compared independently with its minimum in thresholds.schema.json, and no average, confidence or mutation result substitutes for a low dimension. Level 0 means a demonstrated contradiction; a missing observation is an evidence error, never a zero. The canonical instance is law/policy/soft-gate-rubric.json, serialized under DEVAI-CANONICAL-JSON-V1, and soft-gate evidence binds its digest as rubric_sha256.",
      "reference": "ADR-MDL-0004",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 56,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": []
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/soft-gate-score.schema.json",
      "sha256": "b5339c8aab547081838d37b741099a83bb3bf35361e6dcce60327c7805166584",
      "jsonPointer": "/examples/0/citations/spec_coherence/0/path",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "law/adr/ADR-MDL-0004-scored-soft-gate.md",
      "reference": "ADR-MDL-0004",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 8,
      "context": {
        "mode": "data-keyword-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "examples"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
