      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/thresholds.schema.json",
      "sha256": "c55e0d8eee22aeb10e361e9b16b2923e30465d3282472fc329d7fefa367c1f7f",
      "jsonPointer": "/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Hard and scored soft gate thresholds, held canonically in law/policy/thresholds.json and installed for adopters as .devai/config/thresholds.json. coverage, mutation, lint, typecheck and freshness are the original hard thresholds, which ADR-MDL-0004 leaves unchanged; coverage and mutation percentages are never soft thresholds and review confidence is never a rubric score. soft_gate pins the scored soft gate as constants so a candidate cannot lower them: an integer scale 0 to 4, a minimum of 3 for each of the four rubric dimensions compared independently under all-dimensions aggregation, evidence no older than 24 hours with zero future tolerance, an evaluator independent of the working agent, and an observed completed evaluation with no tools or MCP servers. The consumer binds the exact thresholds bytes it applied as thresholds_sha256 in soft-gate evidence; a changed digest or one dimension below its minimum blocks admission even when the verdict is pass.",
      "reference": "ADR-MDL-0004",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 236,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": []
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/triage-breaker.schema.json",
      "sha256": "6241a0dab9c590388cf46e177124833816ee96b75ba1e36536bf93db30105856",
      "jsonPointer": "/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "The document the Article 23 cross-family tie-breaker reply must carry under ADR-MDL-0001. Its one consumer is tieBreakWithLadder in packages/loop/src/loop/triage.ts, which asks a model from another family to vote between two disagreeing triage classifications and validates the reply through the one shared extractor in the model bridge. The classification vocabulary is the triage.schema.json classification enum; a vote that matches one candidate makes that candidate the resolution, and any other vote, including inconclusive, escalates to a human under Article 19. The confidence is a bare number, not the score object a recorded triage verdict carries, because the breaker reply is a vote and not a verdict record. The document is closed so a review verdict or any other shape is refused rather than read as inconclusive; an extractor error outcome keeps a bounded redacted excerpt and the SHA-256 of the full reply.",
      "reference": "ADR-MDL-0001",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 76,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": []
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/use-cases.schema.json",
      "sha256": "b91f08cb71b169290f627cf81a36ea9153314e3c0531a7c251eedd2db20cb59f",
      "jsonPointer": "/$defs/Ref/properties/endpointIds/description",
      "location": "value",
      "originalString": "Endpoint observation references (ADR-SCR-0016). Qualified IDs match exactly; legacy METHOD path aliases resolve only when exactly one API endpoint owns the alias. Ambiguous or stale references require explicit migration and never silently credit multiple source variants. Qualified observation IDs include source evidence and are not stable routing identifiers.",
      "reference": "ADR-SCR-0016",
      "occurrenceIndex": 0,
      "stringOffset": 33,
      "context": {
        "mode": "annotation-value",
        "observedKeywords": [
          "$defs",
          "properties",
          "description"
        ],
        "ancestorSegments": [
          "$defs",
          "Ref",
          "properties",
          "endpointIds"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "law/schemas/workflow-step-inventory.schema.json",
      "sha256": "fba2c4c0a9c2426fd680c3f8bc57b8cc289f3d1a0b0a2c70931c0dbbef654ff8",
